  DELAY1 — one FURTHER day of execution delay, on every 10 bps member.
    The engine already decides at close t and fills at t+1 (PROTOCOL rule 2), and it
    reads the weight frame only on rebalance dates, so shifting the FILLED frame would
    be a one-MONTH lag, not a one-day one.  DELAY1 is therefore built correctly by
    staling the SIGNAL by one trading day at the same rebalance dates: the book is
    decided on close t-1 and filled at t+1.
